   $q$Paragraph 4 says keepers had to be "frugal." Which choice gives the meaning and the clue that supports it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"wealthy and comfortable, because oil was \"expensive\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"good at fixing tools, because spare parts were \"hard to get\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"careful with money and supplies, because they \"wasted nothing\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"lonely and isolated, because boats came \"once a month\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$careful with money and supplies, because they "wasted nothing"$q$, $q$Keepers used oil "carefully and wasted nothing" and repaired instead of replacing, which shows frugal means careful with money and supplies. Fixing tools is one example of being frugal, but it is too narrow to be the whole meaning.$q$, 'draft', 'dea1a239-7b14-599e-9914-0ddbc58f17f7')
