   $q$According to paragraph 1, "ambient" noise is:$q$, $q$[{"text":"the music playing in your headphones","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"},{"text":"the sound of a bus engine only","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"the background sound all around you","is_correct":true},{"text":"a sudden sound that startles you","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$the background sound all around you$q$, $q$The author defines it right after the word: "the background sound that surrounds you wherever you are." An engine rumble is one example of ambient noise, but the word is not limited to buses.$q$, 'draft', '1c44f6ff-cb9f-57e6-8e1d-3b3065baea3f')
