  ('d4371386-b1e2-58a0-99d1-5ff38113ba0b', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-context-clues'), null, 'medium',
   $q$In paragraph 4, Yusuf says a river "ties them together." What does the phrase "ties them together" mean here?$q$, $q$[{"text":"divides the wall into separate sections","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"fastens the scenes to the wall with string","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"connects the scenes so they feel like one whole","is_correct":true},{"text":"makes every scene look exactly the same","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$connects the scenes so they feel like one whole$q$, $q$The river runs "behind every scene," linking them, which answers Ms. Varga's call for a mural that feels like one picture. No real string is involved, so the literal meaning of tying does not fit.$q$, 'draft', '337b6a72-8c9c-5cc9-bd7e-7d39ff42813c')
