   $q$In paragraph 1, the word "endurance" means:$q$, $q$[{"text":"the ability to run in short bursts of speed","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-contrast"},{"text":"the moment a race finally comes to an end","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"surface-association"},{"text":"the ability to keep going for a long time","is_correct":true},{"text":"the distance of a full marathon race","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$the ability to keep going for a long time$q$, $q$The author defines it directly: "the ability to keep going for a long time without stopping." Bursts of speed describe sprinters, who are contrasted with marathon runners.$q$, 'draft', '3cd9f915-b6b7-578f-bfa5-7dd26668d077')
