   $q$Which phrase in paragraph 2 restates the meaning of "deplete"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"using up nearly all of what they had stored\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"which the body stores in the muscles and liver\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opposite-meaning"},{"text":"\"feel as if their legs are made of stone\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"},{"text":"\"After about two hours of hard running\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-context-clue"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"using up nearly all of what they had stored"$q$, $q$The phrase right after "deplete their glycogen" restates it as "using up nearly all of what they had stored." Legs feeling like stone is the result of depleting glycogen, not the meaning of the word.$q$, 'draft', '3cd9f915-b6b7-578f-bfa5-7dd26668d077')
